  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Chlorobutanol is a chemical compound used in medicines as a pharmaceutical preservative, and it is also classified as an antiemetic drug. It appears to be an approved drug, including for veterinary use, though some products containing it have been withdrawn; it is not authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1047468\">Wikidata Q1047468</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>chlorobutanol</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A04AD04</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB11386\">DB11386</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5977\">5977</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:134813\">134813</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1047468\">Q1047468</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C4H7Cl3O</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>177.449 g/mol (PubChem CID 5977)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>2 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
